      "title": "Clean-voice dataset (2 steps)",
      "text": "Step 1: set media_path + video_path, queue. The separator writes the whole-track clean-voice stem <name>_voice.flac (htdemucs_ft default - cleaner vocals, less echo).\n\nStep 2: copy the printed voice_path into the slicer's audio_path widget and queue again. The txt+flac pairs are then cut from the CLEAN VOICE stem while subtitles still come from the original video.\n\nShortcut: the slicer can also separate internally - set its separation_model to htdemucs_ft or htdemucs (and audio_path empty) and every cue yields <timestamp>_voice.flac in ONE run.\n\nBackground stems were removed in v1.4.0 (dub merges drift when a second stem is involved).",
